In article <91138.215602MBS110@psuvm.psu.edu> MBS110@psuvm.psu.edu (That neat guy, Mark Sachs) writes:
>Now the suggestion: This was one of my favorite things from Rogue and I
>wish it was implemented in Nethack. You could hit a key and see a list
>of all the things you've discovered over the course of the game. (For
>example, "A red potion of booze... a puce potion of gain ability...
>a scroll called HACKEM MUCHE of identify" etc.) Absolutely useless, of
>course, but it was still sort of neat. Anyone else think this should
>be added?
>
I have to disagree: that would VERY useful! For example, to write a
scroll with a magic marker, you have to have read that type of scroll,
or else you'll get something you have read. So you need to know what
you've read.
In general, games like this should do everything possible to avoid any
need for the player to use a paper and pencil (that's the whole point of
computers, right - to free us from such drudgery).
This is an excellent suggestion - DEV TEAM TAKE NOTE!


